; =====================================================================
; features.cddl
;
; VERBATIM.  RFC 9165's own CDDL, copied unchanged, margin intact.  NOT
; authored by this project.
;
; Figures 6, 7, 8 and 9 (Section 4) - the four .feature idioms.  They define
; disjoint rule names, so unlike Figures 3 and 4 they share a file.  Each is
; a separate region.
;
; Note Figure 6's `bar = ...` and `baz = ...`: `...` is a PLACEHOLDER in the
; source's prose sense, and `baz`'s trailing comment says so ("complex stuff
; that doesn't all need to be in the detail").  It is not CDDL's `...`
; operator, which RFC 8610 defines only as a range operator between two
; values.  Figure 6 therefore does not parse as CDDL, and that is the source's
; own bytes.  Reported in README.md, never repaired.
;
; Source digest (sha256 of the full cached source text):
;   94f86116c04fde0f11d54576465181090ec33983d78db82527c0703a41976774
; Source: RFC 9165, "Additional Control Operators for the Concise
;         Data Definition Language (CDDL)", C. Bormann, December
;         2021, Standards Track, ISSN 2070-1721.
;         <https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9165.txt>
; =====================================================================

; Figure 6: Providing Explicit Detail with .feature
; ---- BEGIN VERBATIM F-6 (source lines 379-383, sha256 1b1508b5cfe2e6c5209103d795638f9628ba091ababfd0c477349f3e36f188e7) ----
   foo = {
     kind: bar / baz .feature (["foo-extensions", "bazify"])
   }
   bar = ...
   baz = ... ; complex stuff that doesn't all need to be in the detail
; ---- END VERBATIM F-6 ----

; Figure 7: Map Extensibility with .feature
; ---- BEGIN VERBATIM F-7 (source lines 404-411, sha256 75460c424e300507944d8bdeb3887daa9be649f77f542128f0506a816e123097) ----
   person = {
     ? name: text
     ? organization: text
     $$person-extensions
     * (text .feature "further-person-extension") => any
   }

   $$person-extensions //= (? bloodgroup: text)
; ---- END VERBATIM F-7 ----

; Figure 8: Type Extensibility with .feature
; ---- BEGIN VERBATIM F-8 (source lines 418-420, sha256 3ba4a9adab29594beea9c05a56100e4a4a8bedb4106cc5f84a26830387ef6039) ----
   allowed-types = number / text / bool / null
                 / [* number] / [* text] / [* bool]
                 / (any .feature "allowed-type-extension")
; ---- END VERBATIM F-8 ----

; Figure 9: Describing Variants with .feature
; ---- BEGIN VERBATIM F-9 (source lines 433-439, sha256 9eeaf182affef26b5e46dfff6ce7b572b0bf4baa7e5c4950da07541d4cd5bdfa) ----
   SenML-Record = {
   ; ...
     ? v => number
   ; ...
   }
   v = JC<"v", 2>
   JC<J,C> = J .feature "json" / C .feature "cbor"
; ---- END VERBATIM F-9 ----
